{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793886721,"nonce":"HJCZtIJ+Vz0VkRPRtfQCNXR4IkE=","message":"Implemented candidate-first scalarization setup. scalar_replace_alloc discovers allocation-bearing blocks before building constant/use indexes, with one shared candidate predicate. heap_scalarize collects fixed-size allocation roots first and skips cast/alias/phi indexes when none exist. Rewrites, ownership checks, block order and fixed-point round counts are unchanged.\n\nValidation: 31 focused compiler tests passed (5 scalar replacement, 2 allocation audit, 13 heap scalarization, 11 partial escape), exercising interpreter, Cranelift and LLVM where supported. The new audit fixture runs four candidate-free arithmetic/cast/phi sweeps with zero Rust allocations/reallocations and unchanged serialized HIR. A cross-block fixture verifies uses in allocation-free blocks still prevent unsound local scalarization. Lua 46 conformance groups including full official suites, Python 50 groups, foreign tests and native-snapshot checks passed. TS local execution: 1413 PASS across interpreter/baseline/LLVM; full pinned official corpus: 5948/5948 files, 6825 cases, PASS1151 FAIL12 UNSUPPORTED2234 SKIP3428, regressions=[]; all case verdicts/options and coverage equal the previous validated run. No baseline edits. All-target clippy with LLVM/allocation audit, formatting and diff checks passed.\n\nNUC: baseline frozen 25e174968cf9af5101292b738322d5a6e03999cf binary versus candidate frozen binary; LLVM disabled by absence of ZYLUA_LLVM, default release policy, native snapshots enabled, affinity CPUs0/2/4/6. Both builds finished before timing. Shared lock, per-sample no-Cargo/rustc gate, thermal/load gates, all reference checks matched. Initial nine-case run: 7 alternating pairs each, 126 samples, zero throttle deltas. Median wall ms before -\u003e after:\nmethod_call: 28.175 -\u003e 28.078\nop_overload: 31.818 -\u003e 32.688\nbinary_trees: 144.764 -\u003e 153.627\nrecords: 81.082 -\u003e 80.284\npipeline: 316.810 -\u003e 318.456\ntokenize: 104.767 -\u003e 103.474\ncollatz: 142.693 -\u003e 142.662\nmethod_short: 19.615 -\u003e 18.764\nmethod_long: 45.515 -\u003e 46.405\n\nFollowed the slower-looking cases with 21 fresh alternating pairs each, another 126 samples with matching references and zero throttle deltas. Paired-median-ratio bootstrap intervals (exploratory, not a broad throughput claim):\nop_overload: 32.464 -\u003e 31.703 ms; paired change +0.05%, interval [-4.50%, +1.29%].\nbinary_trees: 144.781 -\u003e 146.308 ms; paired change +0.80%, interval [-0.08%, +2.67%].\nmethod_long: 45.844 -\u003e 45.687 ms; paired change -0.65%, interval [-0.97%, +0.52%].\n\nThe apparent long-method slowdown did not repeat. Binary-trees remains slightly slower by median with uncertainty spanning no change. Do not claim broad wall-time improvements. These guards remove allocations in functions without candidates; the hot main bodies still contain mallocs and their preparation totals remain largely unchanged. The next lazy cross-block-index opportunity is recorded on parent 1be184c, which stays open.\n\nIR review: 18 local optimized bodies; 15 text-identical after raw-ID normalization, 3 differing only in reviewed hoisted load/GEP ordering with consistent SSA renaming. All five kernels had matching outputs. NUC method_long captures with normal OSR/native snapshots: main1041, resume region585, adapter10 CLIF instructions, identical per-opcode counts in three captures per binary; all six placed119 native functions. Four timed main-body traces per arm for method_call/op_overload/records/tokenize have identical optimizer progress/round sequences. Example method_call timed phase totals8.580 -\u003e8.515ms, scalar_replace_alloc0.475 -\u003e0.460, heap_scalarize0.765 -\u003e0.750. These instrumented traces disable OSR on both arms and are separate from ordinary wall measurements.\n\nExcluded evidence: three earlier partial timing runs aborted upon detecting unrelated Cargo activity (one identified as blinc_app CSS hot reload). They are preserved but excluded from the verdict. During later OSR-disabled diagnostics, the third baseline collatz run hit thermal throttling; that diagnostic sweep stopped and collatz is excluded from phase-timing conclusions. The ordinary nine-case collatz timings were clean. The subsequent 21-pair controls waited for cooldown and passed all gates. No workload was terminated or unrelated checkout modified.\n\nArtifacts: /private/tmp/zyntax-scalarize-setup, including source/binary hashes, test logs, full TS reports, IR comparisons, NUC samples/thermal logs and analysis scripts. NUC evidence archive SHA256 fbae3bd20c56cf1c54b08f7298323e20d2f0e22b8058a9394319cd5049fa9089. Frozen binaries and isolated source remain on the NUC; coordination lock released.","files":null}]}